{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_12-22-18-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nd={\\\"rationale\\\":(\\\"Adds three over-subscribed cases to the shutdown probe to test one part of the mechanism explanation. The corrected Fact says a VerifyLeader caller is stranded because its send into the buffered verifyCh is accepted by a slot nobody will drain, so a send that cannot be accepted - because every slot is already taken - should be saved by the shutdown case instead. The new cases issue 320 concurrent VerifyLeader calls, five times the 64 slots, and compare their post-shutdown outcomes against the 128-call cases that already strand. If over-subscription protects later callers the multi-case comparison holds; if it does not, the receipt says the strand does not depend on how full the channel is when the loop exits. Execution is requested and no outcome is claimed in advance.\\\"),\n \\\"experiment\\\":{\\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"b2ccc787c9384b008b5f9c668746f760-question-0\\\",\\\"harness_path\\\":\\\"assurance_generated_test.go\\\",\n  \\\"previous_id\\\":\\\"9bc3e6d5ea9c4b298e4a229e13b8f86d-experiment\\\",\n  \\\"revision_reason\\\":\\\"The previous revision pinned the strand to channel buffering by enabling BatchApplyCh. This revision adds three VerifyLeader cases that issue 320 concurrent calls - five times the verifyCh capacity - so a share of the sends cannot be accepted, and it takes the number of calls as a parameter so the 128-call cases remain as the comparison. Event names and measured fields are unchanged; the call count is already carried in both events.\\\",\n  \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"api_verify_future\\\",\\\"defer_error_block\\\",\\\"verify_channel_buffer\\\",\\\"shutdown_close\\\",\\\"apply_channel_unbuffered\\\",\\\"batch_apply_ch_config\\\"],\n  \\\"scope\\\":{\\\"description\\\":\\\"Run the shutdown probe with 128 calls for VerifyLeader, Barrier and Apply, the batched BatchApplyCh cases, the no-shutdown controls, and three additional VerifyLeader cases with 320 concurrent calls, recording for each case how many futures are left incomplete in the racing phase and how many of the eight post-shutdown calls are answered within 500ms.\\\",\n   \\\"assumptions\\\":[\\\"verifyCh is created with 64 slots, so 320 concurrent senders cannot all be accepted and the surplus senders can only proceed through the shutdown case once shutdown closes the channel.\\\",\n    \\\"Single-voter node, in-memory transport, 50ms timeouts, one process, as in the earlier revisions.\\\",\n    \\\"A single run per case kind is not a rate estimate; the comparison is between call counts under otherwise identical conditions.\\\"],\n   \\\"excluded\\\":[\\\"Buffer sizes other than the fixed 64 slots, and multi-node behaviour.\\\"]},\n  \\\"prefix\\\":(\\\"Each case starts one real Raft instance with its own InmemStore, InmemSnapshotStore and InmemTransport, bootstrapped as a single Voter with HeartbeatTimeout = ElectionTimeout = LeaderLeaseTimeout = 50ms, and waits until it reports Leader. It emits assurance_shutdown_setup carrying trial, kind, shutdown, batch_apply_ch, the call count and the window, then issues the configured number of calls of the chosen kind from separate goroutines, each waiting on Error() with a 4000ms deadline; in the shutdown cases a goroutine calls Shutdown() 2ms into the fill. After Shutdown returns it issues 8 further calls of the same kind one at a time with a 500ms wait each and emits assurance_shutdown_result with the racing counts, the post-phase counts and histograms, the shutdown error, the node state and batch_apply_ch. The over-subscribed cases use trial identifiers 200-202 with 320 VerifyLeader calls. The harness is TestAssuranceShutdownFutureCompletion.\\\"),\n  \\\"prerequisites\\\":[{\\\"alias\\\":\\\"setup\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"assurance_shutdown_setup\\\"}],\n  \\\"comparisons\\\":[\n   {\\\"event\\\":\\\"assurance_shutdown_result\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"trial\\\",\\\"kind\\\",\\\"batch_apply_ch\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"setup\\\",\n    \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"post_responded\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},\n    \\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"shutdown\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"kind\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"verify\\\"},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"calls\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":320}],\n    \\\"description\\\":\\\"Over-subscribed VerifyLeader: whether every post-shutdown call is answered when the channel cannot accept all of the racing sends. Holds would mean the strand depends on spare channel capacity.\\\"},\n   {\\\"event\\\":\\\"assurance_shutdown_result\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"trial\\\",\\\"kind\\\",\\\"batch_apply_ch\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"setup\\\",\n    \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"post_responded\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":False},\n    \\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"shutdown\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"kind\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"verify\\\"},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"calls\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":128}],\n    \\\"description\\\":\\\"The 128-call VerifyLeader cases, where some post-shutdown calls are left unanswered, as the standing comparison.\\\"}]}}\njson.dump(d,open('update.json','w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False); open('update.json','a').write('\\\\n')\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_12-22-18-hashicorp_raft-real-run --submission update.json 2>&1 | tail -2\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
